{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021181-hurt-locker-new-framing-scenes","id":1021181,"title":"[Hurt Locker] New Framing Scenes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T00:28:19-08:00","id":1021181,"title":"[Hurt Locker] New Framing Scenes","content":"Reading now <b>Hurt Locker</b>, I <i>adore</i> some of it\u2019s mechanics ideas. One of them are Framing Scenes which are \u2018mechanics for scenes environment\u2019 \u2013 if you ever wondered what advantages and problems could make combat in kitchen, street in pouring rain or on roof of speeding trains, this section of sourcebook is for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As we only got some few examples of Framing Scenes in book, let\u2019s make our own. I will start with some more typical and less extreme, but I think that those could be widely use, as they are part of most stories in <b>CoD</b> I ran. Any help or new ideas are, as always, welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>High Noon</b></span><br /> <br /> It\u2019s a high noon on sunny day. Sun is blazing, making everything crystal clear. In XIX century, on some town\u2019s main street, some two gun men could made a showdown in a weather like this.<br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Weather and clear vision makes ranged attacks more easier - Take +1 bonus on those.<br /> <b>Penalty: </b>The sun show all wicked - any Stealth based actions take -2 penalty, because of short shadows and light all around.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Optional \u2014 accept it for a Beat, if you want. Your character turned or moved unfortunately and is now blinded by the sun - take Blinded Tilt. Character can Resolve it by spending whole turn to hide his eyes from it and getting them to rest few seconds.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Dead of Night</b></span><br /> <br /> This is dark night, long past lights of human settlements. Darkness entrench you and every tree or stone can become monster you unsuspecting. Your only friend is pale light of the Moon. If he show you his face, that is\u2026<br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Darkness all around you make sneaking much easier \u2013 you get +1 bonus to Stealth base actions. If there is no Moon or any other light source to be seen, it get\u2019s up to +2 bonus.<br /> <b>Penalty: </b> You cannot hit what you do not see \u2013 any direct attack actions gets -1 penalty if there is Moon or other light source. If there is no light, penalty goes up to -2 in the end.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> You missed a branch or slipped on stone \u2013 whichever, you hit a ground. Hard. You have Knockdown Condition now and need to use full action to return to normal position from prone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-23-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:01:24-08:00","id":1023216,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a>, you are the author of this subsystem, yes? Maybe you have some cool Framing Scenes to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:31:17-08:00","id":1023231,"title":"","content":"I have <b>got </b>to pick up Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> Without being able to check for redundancy or compare with others, here's one:<br /> <br /> <b>L'Heure Bleue</b><br /> In the twilight of early dawn or late dusk, the rays of the sun are scattered across the skies to produce a profound atmosphere in this &quot;blue hour&quot;. While mostly treasured as a romantic and artistic moment, it is also called <i>L'Heure entre Chien et Loup</i>, or &quot;The Hour of the Dog and the Wolf&quot;, where it is the time of obscurity where you cannot say for sure whether the animal approaching you is your loyal dog or a hungry wolf.<br /> <b>Advantage</b>: The romantic atmosphere gives a +1 bonus to Expression rolls involving art.<br /> <b>Penalty</b>: The vista does a good job of catching one's eyes, and imposes a -1 to perception rolls.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Humans are not the only ones enjoying this liminal hour, where the mundane blends with the fantastic. You gain the Reception Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T05:33:54-08:00","id":1024241,"title":"","content":"Preparing to use in my nearest session one of greatest tropes of horror storytelling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Dark Dungeon</b></span><br /> You are entombed in tight, dark tunnels. Air is moist and smell of old, light is sparse if even any made by few torches or lamps. Maybe one or two persons at most can walk side by side and walls are slippery. Ground is hard and cold. You are only beings in this place\u2026<br /> <b>Advantage: </b>Darkness all around you make sneaking much easier \u2013 you get +1 bonus to Stealth base actions even if are some light sources. If there isn\u2019t any, it get\u2019s up to +2 bonus.<br /> <b>Penalty: </b> You cannot hit what you do not see \u2013 any direct attack actions gets -1 penalty if there are only limited light sources. If there is no light, penalty goes up to -2 in the end.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> You slipped on stone or fell on the nearest wall \u2013 whichever, you hit a ground. Hard. You have Knockdown Condition now and need to use full action to return to normal position from prone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:06:07-08:00","id":1024294,"title":"","content":"The Dark Dungeon frame's mechanical effects are the same as the Dead of Night frame. Editing mistake?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, not <i>exactly </i>the same, but might as well be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:14:32-08:00","id":1024300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021181-hurt-locker-new-framing-scenes?p=1024294#post1024294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Dungeon frame's mechanical effects are the same as the Dead of Night frame. Editing mistake?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Well, not <i>exactly </i>the same, but might as well be.</div> </div> </div> </div>From logical reasons - they work the same. I really thought about it, and mechanics should work a lot like. If you have other proposition on it, I'm all ears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:31:05-08:00","id":1024308,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Dark Dungeon</b></span><br /> You are entombed in tight, dark tunnels. The air is moist and smells of mold. Light is sparse, only with a few torches or lamps to feed it. The corridors are tight, with two people at most able to walk side-by-side, but there are small niches and dents in the walls slippery with moss. You are only beings in this place, and surely those light stepping sounds amongst the echoing breeze must be figments of your anxiety...<br /> <b>Advantage</b>: The darkness and the haphazard walls give you ample hiding space. You gain a +1 to all ambush attempts, which becomes a +2 in patches of complete darkness, a particularly large cavity in the walls or a hidden fork in the corridors.<br /> <b>Penalty</b>: You become paranoid of what might lie beyond your immediate range of vision. You suffer a -2 to Initiative due to progressing slowly in a poorly lit and tight area..<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Worries turn to reality. You are ambushed by a hostile entity. Pray it is a human or an animal.<br /> <br /> Changed the fluff just a bit slightly to accomodate the mechanics. My version focuses on the ambushing part, rather than the moving sneakily part. Both are about stealth, so I can see both frames applied to inflict merry hell for those trying to walk through it. (If the rules allow for it, that is. Like I said, I'm doing this without reading Hurt Locker.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:14:34-08:00","id":1024342,"title":"","content":"I would still stick to Stealth ( or other Skills based ) actions bonus - it's much more open to interpretation, as ambush is only one of them. I can see whole paranoia and Initiative angel, and generally agree. I would surely change Dramatic Failure as it should be Condition or Tilt mechanics - being ambushed is more plot thing than mechanics - you will be ambushed only if ST made antagonist there for you to be ambushed. And <b>Hurt Locker</b> points that Dramatic Failures should be Conditions or Tilts, in most cases. For Dark Dungeons scenes, maybe adding some paranoia related Condition? Maybe... Spooked! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:00:32-08:00","id":1024564,"title":"","content":"Oh, so they have to be Conditions or Tilts, huh? In that case, yes, I'd go for Spooked. That's the Condition that nudges you into taking a closer look at something scary. right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T00:56:53-08:00","id":1024660,"title":"","content":"Quick template on Framing Scenes in book is this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hurt Locker, p. 22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Advantage:</b> The environment provides a +2 bonus to rolls able to take advantage of it, as long as the player is willing to accept a dramatic failure in return. The Storyteller decides based on the description of the scene. She can do this on the fly if she likes.<br /> <b>Penalty:</b> The environment imposes a \u20132 penalty to a category of other actions. Again, the Storyteller can decide ahead of time, or on the fly.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Basic dramatic failure imposes a Tilt selected by the Storyteller or another disadvantageous Condition. The dramatic failure only applies when a character harnesses the framing scene\u2019s advantage. In some situations the player can decide whether to suffer a dramatic failure to earn a Beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>As to Spooked, <b>CoD Rulebook</b> says this on this Condition matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 291</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spooked</b><br /> Your character has seen something supernatural \u2014 not overt enough to terrify her, but unmistakably otherworldly.<br /> How your character responds to this is up to you, but it captivates her and eats her attention. You can shed this Condition when your character\u2019s fear and fascination causes her to do something that hinders the group or complicates things (she goes off alone to investigate a strange noise, stays up all night researching, runs away instead of holding her ground, etc.).<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Shed the Condition as noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>But more reading about it, I think that Shaken is much more appropriate 'paranoia' Condition:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Rulebook, p. 290</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shaken</b><br /> Something has frightened your character extensively. Any time your character is taking an action where that fear might hinder her, you may opt to fail the roll (before you\u2019ve made the roll), and shed this Condition. This Condition can be imposed by a successful breaking point roll.<br /> <b>Example Skills:</b> Brawl, Firearms, Intimidation, Weaponry<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Fail a roll, as noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or could be both being able to take by character - both seems appropriate to 'weird things going in dark tunnel', and there is nothing wrong from taking one or another - character still will have one Condition on her from Dramatic Failure, don't she.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T01:35:52-08:00","id":1024668,"title":"","content":"The dramatic failure option is only available when the characters take advantage of the frame? Hmm... then my suggestions probably need some refining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T19:41:21-08:00","id":1028380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021181-hurt-locker-new-framing-scenes?p=1023216#post1023216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a>, you are the author of this subsystem, yes? Maybe you have some cool Framing Scenes to share?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not. That was the inimitable David Hill, and it's one of my favorite subsystems of all time. I'm drawing heavy influence from it for my own game, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T20:56:55-08:00","id":1028414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021181-hurt-locker-new-framing-scenes?p=1028380#post1028380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not. That was the inimitable David Hill, and it's one of my favorite subsystems of all time. I'm drawing heavy influence from it for my own game, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I didn't write them. Malcolm wrote them. I designed the basic idea, and came up with the first example to work from. But he fleshed out that basic concept into something super cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}